<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Memory thoughts: created by an event, expiring after a duration, stacking up to a limit with a
  diminishing multiplier per extra copy so a repeated event saturates rather than growing without
  bound. Mood is the difficulty base plus the sum of these, approached by drift.
-->
<Defs>

  <!-- A break is self-limiting: the aftermath lifts mood clear of the threshold. -->
  <ThoughtDef>
    <defName>Thought_Catharsis</defName>
    <moodOffset>150</moodOffset>
    <durationTicks>30000</durationTicks>
  </ThoughtDef>

  <ThoughtDef>
    <defName>Thought_AteMeal</defName>
    <moodOffset>20</moodOffset>
    <durationTicks>15000</durationTicks>
    <stackLimit>2</stackLimit>
  </ThoughtDef>

  <ThoughtDef>
    <defName>Thought_SleptOnGround</defName>
    <moodOffset>-40</moodOffset>
    <durationTicks>15000</durationTicks>
  </ThoughtDef>

  <!--
    U29. Riding a floor down when it collapses. Worse than a night on the ground and shorter
    lived, because it is a fright rather than a grievance; it stacks twice, so a colonist caught
    in a cascade is badly shaken and not indefinitely so.

    It stands in for an injury that cannot exist yet: a-02 has the fall-damage number and there
    is no health model to apply it to (owner, 2026-09-17). When there is, this thought stays -
    being dropped through a floor is worth remembering whether or not it broke anything.
  -->
  <ThoughtDef>
    <defName>Thought_Fell</defName>
    <moodOffset>-60</moodOffset>
    <durationTicks>20000</durationTicks>
    <stackLimit>2</stackLimit>
  </ThoughtDef>

  <!--
    Design 28 §8. Waking from a night outside the temperature bands - remembered, not
    situational, because it is about the night that happened rather than the morning it left
    behind. The situational side of being cold is a banded mood offset on the needs interval and
    never a stored thought at all.

    Milder than a night on the ground (it stacks with it, and SleptOnGround's -40 is the worse
    half of sleeping rough), longer lived because a bad night's ache outlasts the morning.
  -->
  <ThoughtDef>
    <defName>Thought_SleptCold</defName>
    <moodOffset>-30</moodOffset>
    <durationTicks>20000</durationTicks>
  </ThoughtDef>

  <ThoughtDef>
    <defName>Thought_SleptHot</defName>
    <moodOffset>-30</moodOffset>
    <durationTicks>20000</durationTicks>
  </ThoughtDef>

  <!--
    Design 33 §12, friendly fire (the owner's row: "the victim remembers being attacked (-8, one
    day); any colonist's death is felt by every colonist (-6, three days); no opinions yet").
    The owner's points are on a mood of a hundred and these are thousandths, so -8 is -80.

    Attacked: given for every swing by a colonist that reaches her - a hit, a miss or a dodge alike
    (section 14f; the owner, 2026-09-24: a missed swing counts) - and only once while it lasts. A
    second swing renews it, so the day runs from the latest one (renewsOnRepeat, section 14e; the
    owner left it to us and we recommended it); no other thought renews. A memory names no other
    pawn, so two attackers are one grievance; that is "no opinions yet" in the data.

    Died: every other colonist, for three days (60000 ticks a day). Stacks three deep at the usual
    diminishing multiplier (-60, -45, -33), so a massacre takes a content colony to the edge of a
    break and not over it on its own. The limit is ours, to be tuned after a play.
  -->
  <ThoughtDef>
    <defName>Thought_AttackedByColonist</defName>
    <moodOffset>-80</moodOffset>
    <durationTicks>60000</durationTicks>
    <renewsOnRepeat>true</renewsOnRepeat>
  </ThoughtDef>

  <ThoughtDef>
    <defName>Thought_ColonistDied</defName>
    <moodOffset>-60</moodOffset>
    <durationTicks>180000</durationTicks>
    <stackLimit>3</stackLimit>
  </ThoughtDef>

</Defs>
